cgst-s24.plainEnglish:
**Section 24 lists persons who must register regardless of turnover** (subject to
section 23):
- persons making **inter-State taxable supply** of goods (services up to 20 lakh
  are exempted by notification);
- **casual taxable persons** and **non-resident taxable persons**;
- persons liable to pay under **reverse charge**;
- persons liable under **section 9(5)** (e-commerce operators for notified
  services);
- persons required to **deduct TDS** (section 51) or **collect TCS**
  (section 52);
- **agents** supplying on behalf of other taxable persons;
- **Input Service Distributors**;
- persons who supply through an **e-commerce operator** required to collect TCS
  (with a relaxation for small intra-State goods suppliers);
- every **e-commerce operator**;
- persons supplying **OIDAR** services from outside India to unregistered
  persons in India;
- persons supplying **online money gaming** from outside India to a person in
  India.

cgst-s38.plainEnglish:
**Section 38 (substituted from 01.10.2022) is the framework for the auto-drafted
inward-supply statement and for restricting ITC.**

It replaces the old GSTR-2 / GSTR-2A "matching" scheme with a **communicated
statement of eligible and ineligible ITC** (operationalised as **GSTR-2B**). The
section lets the rules specify circumstances in which ITC in respect of a
supplier is **not available** to the recipient — for example, where the supplier:
- is a new registrant (within a prescribed period);
- has defaulted in payment of tax beyond a prescribed period / amount;
- has short-paid output tax vs GSTR-3B beyond a threshold;
- has taken excess ITC vs GSTR-2B beyond a threshold;
- is a person restricted from using the credit ledger under Rule 86B; or
- is otherwise a class of persons as prescribed.

cgst-s79.plainEnglish:
**Section 79 is the recovery machinery** for amounts payable but not paid. The
proper officer may:
- **(a)** deduct from money owed to the person (refunds, other dues);
- **(b)** detain and sell goods under his control;
- **(c)** issue a **garnishee notice (DRC-13)** to a person who owes money to the
  defaulter — banks, customers, debtors — requiring them to pay the department;
- **(d)** distrain and sell movable / immovable property;
- **(e)** recover as **arrears of land revenue** through the District Collector;
- **(f)** apply to a Magistrate to recover as a fine.

**Instalments** — the Commissioner may allow payment in up to **24 monthly
instalments** with interest, except for self-assessed tax (section 80).
Recovery of a **cross-empowered** dues (CGST / SGST) is coordinated.

igst-s12.plainEnglish:
**Section 12 — place of supply of services where BOTH supplier and recipient are
in India.**

- **General rule (12(2))** — to a **registered** person: his location; to an
  **unregistered** person: the address on record, else the supplier's location.
- **Special rules** override the general rule for:
  - **immovable property / lodging / event venue** (12(3)) — where the property /
    venue is;
  - **restaurant, catering, personal grooming, fitness, beauty, health**
    (12(4)) — where performed;
  - **training and performance appraisal** (12(5));
  - **admission to an event / amusement park** (12(6)) — where the event is held;
  - **organisation of an event** (12(7)) — recipient's location (if registered),
    else where held;
  - **transport of goods, including mail / courier** (12(8)) — recipient's
    location (registered) / where goods are handed over (unregistered);
    **proviso**: where the destination is outside India, place of supply is the
    **destination of the goods**;
  - **passenger transport** (12(9)), **services on board a conveyance**
    (12(10)), **telecom** (12(11)), **banking / financial / insurance** (12(12)),
    **advertisement to Government** (12(14)).

igst-s13.plainEnglish:
**Section 13 — place of supply of services where the supplier OR the recipient is
outside India** (cross-border services).

- **General rule (13(2))** — location of the **recipient**; if not available, the
  supplier's location.
- **Special rules**:
  - **13(3)** — services requiring physical presence of goods (repairs,
    testing) → where performed; services to an individual requiring his physical
    presence → where performed;
  - **13(4)** — immovable property → where the property is;
  - **13(5)** — admission to / organisation of events → where held;
  - **13(8)** — **(a)** banking company / financial institution services to
    account holders, **(b) intermediary services**, **(c)** hiring of means of
    transport up to one month → **location of the supplier**;
  - **13(9)** — transport of goods (other than mail / courier) → **destination of
    the goods**;
  - **13(11)** — OIDAR services → location of the recipient.
